times look in the changelog of a game or app and it just says \"Multiple improvements in stability and bug fixes\" and you think, \"Give me details!\"? Well, this is one of those.\n\n**Fix** Unexpected API errors are now answered in JSON when the calling tool asked for JSON output. A details request with an invalid ID gets a proper &quot;invalid ID&quot; error.\n\n**Fix** If you use a Torbox indexer, NZBHydra2 no longer keeps two extra threads running for every config save that followed a Torbox search.\n\n**Fix** When a server stopped sending in the middle of a response, NZBHydra2 now reports the timeout or dropped connection instead of a confusing parsing error.\n\n**Fix** An error in NZBHydra2&apos;s own handling of search results no longer disables the indexer. A search response that could not be read no longer counts twice against the indexer&apos;s API limit.\n\n**Fix** Configuring Sonarr 5 under External tools no longer fails with &quot;unsupported Sonarr version&quot;. Future major versions of Sonarr and Radarr are no longer rejected either.\n\n","upstream_url":"https://github.com/theotherp/nzbhydra2/releases/tag/v9.3.2"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","HOME=/root","LANGUAGE=en_US.UTF-8","LANG=en_US.UTF-8","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true","NZBHYDRA2_RELEASE_TYPE=Release","DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive"],"exposed_ports":["5076/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/nzbhydra2/builds/v9.3.2-ls9.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/nzbhydra2/builds/v9.3.2-ls9/diff.json","layers":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/nzbhydra2/builds/v9.3.2-ls9/layers.amd64.json","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playg